<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — Model fidelity to source: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "E1-E3 (`log_spiral_r`, `whorl_expansion`, `gnomon_radius`, L112-L131), E4-E6 screw accretion (`grow_tooth`, L146-L181), E8-E9 St Venant warping (`tri_warp`, `ellipse_warp`, `st_venant_triangle_field`, L186-L223) and E7 helix (L228-L242) are implemented as published and mirrored by 17 Lean theorems, but the specimen test uses only the 2-D plane-spiral special case; the twisted (τ > 0) model that Thompson invokes for long tusks is rendered, never fitted." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py L445–L470: run_analysis fits only the plane log spiral + circle; τ > 0 helico-spiral never fitted to the projected centreline <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0e7e77bc1/thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py#L445-L470>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 6.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L736-L755) returns 11 measurements with one literature reference (Kiladze & Chernova 2018, z = +1.0 within 2 SD) and a St Venant sector count against theory, plus CV(κ·w) < CV(κ) (3.59 vs 12.0); but the KS statistic is a two-sample test between the spiral and circle residual sets (p = 0 is uninformative), there is no bootstrap CI on ψ or on the groove angle, no shuffled-width control for the accretion law, and no along-shaft test of tan α vs 1/d." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py L378–L391: accretion statistics without bootstrap or shuffle control <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0e7e77bc1/thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py#L378-L391>",
        "thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py L459–L466: two-sample KS between residual sets instead of a one-sample residual normality / CV test <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0e7e77bc1/thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py#L459-L466>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-circle-null-rmse-px>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-cv-kappa-w-accretion-law>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-kappa-sign-changes>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-ks-pvalue-spiral-vs-circle-residuals>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-log-spiral-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-log-spiral-psi-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-log-spiral-rmse-px>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-narwhal-alpha-equiv-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-narwhal-tan-alpha-equiv>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-narwhal-z-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-measurement-st-venant-sign-sectors>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — MorphoEval overall 60.7/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 baseline of `t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py` (overall ~60.7/100). Implements E1-E9 (equiangular spiral, accretion curvature law, screw accretion, St Venant warping and uniform-torsion helix), segments the SHA-256-locked mammoth tusk, fits a log spiral about a searched pole against a circle null (RMSE 37.3 vs 41.8 px, r = 0.963), measures narwhal groove inclination by structure tensor (α ≡ 70.2° vs 66.9 ± 3.3° published, z = +1.0) and reproduces the six-sector St Venant torsion curves. Weaknesses: the 3-D screw model is never fitted to the specimen, curvature changes sign three times so the plane-spiral reading fails, regimes are five hand-picked points, statistics are thin (two-sample KS misuse, no CI / bootstrap, no ablation controls beyond the circle fit), no CLI parameterisation. Overall 60.7/100 (faithfulness 53.1, reproducibility 78.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0e7e77bc1; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scikit-image 0.26.0, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 62, Morphological realism / specimen match 50, Parameter expressivity 40, Morphometric validation 55, Source and data traceability 85, Code-to-model traceability 80, Reproducibility package 72. Output judged: docs/media/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_comparison.png: rendered output of thompson/claims/t1917-032_the-shapes-of-horns-and-of-teeth-or-tusks.py at 0e7e77bc1, image/png, 901553 B, 2200×1265 px, artifact_sha256 ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8 (sha256 ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8), spec_fingerprint d3a3c036d2236fa5e48fed4d773ebe5efc0177f2fb7ef111e8e3fe7dfc6e5241. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: d3a3c036d2236fa5e48fed4d773ebe5efc0177f2fb7ef111e8e3fe7dfc6e5241; artifact_sha256: ce504b6b180f886e2d607acf30623c6aa5ed49ff489607778ef4157b67be39f8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/kiladze2018_narwhal_spiral_table1.csv=f1e9d5a363772f32..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/mammuthus_primigenius_tusk_specimen.jpg=cd33e02d49367204..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/monodon_monoceros_tusk_spiral_specimen.jpg=3c0e4ccdd686c45b..., datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-032/t1917_032_the_shapes_of_horns_and_of_tee_reference.json=6225b4ee87df718c...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Thompson pp. 619, 633-634: constant growth-rate ratio across the basal zone yields a logarithmic spiral; tooth, tusk, beak, claw all follow it; elephant tusk tip ~ spiral pole; long tusks (mammoth, Babirussa) are curves of double curvature | Thompson pp. 621-623 + Fig. 321: St Venant torsion warps non-circular prisms into anticlastic surfaces whose contour lines explain the sinuous growth lines of trihedral horns; reconstructed_in_script: Algebraic accretion law κ = (v_max − v_min)/(w v̄) = Δ/w and its gnomonic closure sin ψ = Δ/c (E4-E5) | Screw-accretion frame update Ω = κ b + τ n generating circle / log spiral / helix / helico-spiral (E6) | Kiladze chord ratio tan α = π/(2 tan φ) conversion from a locally measured groove inclination (E7); transfer_boundary: The narwhal tusk is a labelled analogue for the torsion component; Thompson's 1917 chapter never names the narwhal | A single 2-D museum photograph projects a 3-D helico-spiral tusk; plane-spiral tests are projection-limited; does_not_claim: No growth-rate (v_max, v_min) or CT data: λ and Δ are inferred from geometry, not measured | No handedness determination from the narwhal photograph (tip orientation unknown)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add a systematic parameter-regime sweep over ψ (20-85°), λ, taper c and τ demonstrating the Lean-proved monotonicities numerically and rendering a morphospace panel.",
        "remediation needed: Add negative / ablation controls: Archimedean spiral fit, shuffled-width control for CV(κ·w), τ = 0 ablation, circular-section (a = b) St Venant null.",
        "remediation needed: Fit the 3-D screw-accretion model (E6: ψ or Δ/c, twist τ, taper, view rotation, scale) to the projected mammoth centreline and compare nested τ = 0 (plane spiral) vs τ > 0 (helico-spiral) by RMSE / AIC to test Thompson's 'curve of double curvature'.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the two-sample KS misuse by a one-sample KS on standardised residuals; add bootstrap CIs for ψ, Pearson r and the narwhal groove angle; regress tan α on 1/d along the shaft for the uniform-torsion prediction.",
        "remediation needed: Width-scale the centreline smoothing, expose CLI overrides (--psi, --lam, --taper, --tau, --sigma-frac), and record library versions in result.json." ;
    pk:hasScore 6.07e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

