<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-032-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-032 — teeth & tusks: differential-accretion log spiral + St Venant torsion — Morphological realism / specimen match: 50/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-28"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "HSV segmentation + skeleton longest path recovers the mammoth tusk centreline and width (`segment_mammoth_tusk`, `tusk_centreline_profile`, L247-L328) and the overlay beats the circle null, but the smoothed curvature changes sign 3 times (root bend, straight shaft, reversed tip hook) so the plane log spiral mis-tracks root and tip; the narwhal panel is an analogue; no comparison against Thompson's own tusk description beyond text." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
